Step 3: Qualtrics set up
Step 3 includes all the necessary steps to create the Qualtrics survey/test. We demonstrate the procedure using the PPSE item bank; however, you can follow the same steps using your own item bank. To use the TCAT item bank, additional instructions are provided in the substeps below where necessary.

Step 3.1 - Setup Block
Go to the Qualtrics XM website via your institution and log in with your credentials.
Go to Home page — Create a new project — Survey — and click Get started.
Enter a Name of your choice for the Qualtrics project.





Once you create a new project, modify the default first question. Click on it to select it.
Then from the left panel, under Question Type, choose Text entry type of question.





Change the question text to ‘Test Name’.





Then, click on the three dots at the top right corner of the ‘Test Name’ question and click Copy to create new question of similar type.





Change the text of the second question into ’Access Token’.





These two questions make up a single block, which will be the first block in your test. This block is crucial, as it links the Qualtrics survey to the test specifications you set up in Steps 1 and 2.
Rename the first Block as ‘Setup’ block, by changing the label above the first question.

Then, for the ‘Test Name’ question, select Add requirements and Force response under the Response Requirements options on the left panel.
Similarly, add Force response requirement for the ‘Access Token’ question.

Then, for the ‘Test Name’ question select Default choices from the options on the left panel. Enter the name of your test in the first question as the default choice, and click Save.
Then repeat the process for the second question, entering the access token that you generated previously.






Note



Here we follow the PPSE by entering PPSE as the test name and Tok1234 as the access token. For the TCAT: Enter TCAT as the test name and Tok1234 as the access token.




Then select the ‘Access Token’ question and click the JavaScript option on the left side panel.

Replace the default lines of code in the pop-up window with the script below and click Save.
Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function() {
     this.hideNextButton();
    var that = this;
    (function(){that.clickNextButton();}).delay(1);
});




Step 3.2 Introduction Block (optional)
This block consists of a text question. It is optional and can be used to display introductory text for your study, such as guidelines, ethical approvals, participants’ informed consent, and contact information.

Add a new block by selecting Add Block
Rename the new block as ‘Intro’
Add a new question to the block by selecting Add new question,
and then Text / Graphic type


This does not serve as an actual question; rather, it displays all the necessary information for the test participant.
In this example we add some plain text for illustrative purpose:




Step 3.3 Extra Block (optional)
Similarly to the ‘Intro’ block, you can add an additional block, here labelled as ‘Extra’, with questions you would like to appear before the actual CAT. These may include demographic or other personal questions. In this example, the ‘Extra’ block consists of two questions for illustrative purposes: One asking for the participant’s gender and the other asking for the participant’s age.






Note



No CAT methods are configured for the ‘Extra Block’. All users will be asked the same questions.






Step 3.4 CAT Initialization Block
Similarly,

Add a new block,
Rename it to ‘Init’
Add a new Text / Entry question type,
Enter the phrase ‘Loading…’ as question text.






For the ‘Loading…’ question, select the Javascript option from the left panel.


Replace the default lines of code in the pop-up window with the script below and click Save:
Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function() {
    let answers = {
      // empty for now
  };

  //console.log(answers);
    // CALL
    fetch("https://qualcat.duckdns.org/api/v0/init", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "x-api-key": "${q://QID2/ChoiceTextEntryValue}", // passwrd
      "userid": "${e://Field/SessionID}", // username
      "catName": "${q://QID1/ChoiceTextEntryValue}" // CAT name
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(answers)
  })
  .then(response =&gt; response.json())
  .then(data =&gt; {
    console.log("API returned:", data); // Debug
    // Store the API result in Embedded Data
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("stop_crit", data.stop_crit);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("next_q", data.next_q);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("item_num", data.item_num);
    var arr = data.choices;
    for (var i = 0; i &lt; arr.length; i++) {
        var varName = "choice" + (i + 1);
        Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(varName, arr[i]);
    }
  })
  .catch(err =&gt; console.error("API error:", err));
    this.hideNextButton();
    var that = this;
    (function(){that.clickNextButton();}).delay(4);
});




Step 3.5 Question Block
Add a new block, labelled as ‘Question’.
Then, add a Multiple choice question type.


Select Choices from the left panel and choose the number of response options for your test under Number of choices. Here is set to 5 for the PPSE questionnaire.






Note



For the TCAT: Select 4 number of choices.


Replace the ‘Click to write the question text’ with this line of code ${e://Field/next_q}
Replace the ‘Click to write Choice 1’ with ${e://Field/choice1},‘Click to write Choice 2’ with ${e://Field/choice2} , ‘Click to write Choice 3’ with ${e://Field/choice3} and so on for all available choices.


Next, click the Javascript button on the left side panel, replace the code pasting the following script into the field and click Save:
Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function() {

    // 1. clear Qualtrics internal answer
    this.setChoiceValue("", false);

    // 2. clear any recorded choice values
    var choices = this.getChoices();
    for (var i = 0; i &lt; choices.length; i++) {
        this.setChoiceValue(choices[i], false);
    }

    // 3. clear UI radios
    jQuery("#" + this.questionId + " input[type='radio']").prop("checked", false);
});







Tip



For TCAT, and for maximum-performance test in general you should consider to display the answer choices in a random order. When you make the item bank information file in Step 2, it is convenient to paste all the correct answers into column Choice1 and make the Scores column the same for all the items (e.g. 1000 for dichotomous items).








Warning



For typical-performance test, like the PPSE example we demonstrate here, DO NOT display answers in random order. Please, continue to Step 3.5.



Select the question in the ‘Question’ block.
Select the ‘Choice randomization’ optionin the left side panel.
Then choose ‘Display answers in a random order’ and click ‘Save’.





Step 3.6 - Main CAT Block

Add a new question block
Name it ‘CAT’
Add a new question,
Text/Graphic type of question
Replace the question text with an empty space.
Then, click JavaScript, and replace everything with the following JavaScript code


Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()
{
     let answers = {
    q_resp: "${q://QID7/SelectedChoicesRecode}",
    item_num: "${e://Field/item_num}"
  };

  console.log("API sent:", answers);
    // CALL
    fetch("https://qualcat.duckdns.org/api/v0/cat", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
         "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "x-api-key": "${q://QID2/ChoiceTextEntryValue}", // token
      "userid": "${e://Field/SessionID}", // username
      "catName": "${q://QID1/ChoiceTextEntryValue}" // CAT name
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(answers)
  })
  .then(res =&gt; res.json())
  .then(data =&gt; {
    console.log("API returned:", data); 
    // Store the API result in Embedded Data
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("iter", data.iter);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("next_q", data.item);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("item_num", data.item_num);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("se_thetahat", data.se_thetahat);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("thetahat", data.thetahat);  
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("pat", data.pat);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("J", data.pat.length);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("adm_items", data.iter);
    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData("stop", data.stop); //v0.2
    var arr = data.choices;
    for (var i = 0; i &lt; arr.length; i++) {
        var varName = "choice" + (i + 1);
        Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(varName, arr[i]);
    }
  })
  .catch(err =&gt; console.error("API error:", err));

    this.hideNextButton();
    var that = this;
    (function(){that.clickNextButton();}).delay(1);

});






Warning



Click the drop down Tools Tab and select Show internal IDs.

Make sure that the internal ID of the question in the “Question” block, QID7 in this example, matches the text in the fourth line of the script you entered before (i.e., "${q://QID7/SelectedChoicesRecode}"). If not, edit the script by entering the correct internal ID.












Step 3.7 - Survey Flow Setup
Click the Survey Flow button on the left side bar.

All the question blocks we created before, should be visible in an ordered list as shown below.

In the Init block, click Add Below and select Group.

Rename the new group as ‘Loop’ .
Then in the Question block click the Move button.

Move the Question block under the Loop groupby dragging it.

The Question block is now part of the Loop group.

Similarly, move for the CAT block into the Loop group, under the Question block.

Then click + Add a New Element here under the CAT block, inside the Loop group and select Branch.

Click Add a Condition

Select Embedded Data.

Then,

Enter the word ‘stop’ for the embedded data
Select ‘Is Equal To’ and enter the number ‘1’
Click OK
Add a New Element under the if branch


Select the End of Survey element

The survey flow should now look like this


Now, click the button Duplicate next to the loop group, as many times as the available total number of items. For this example, the PPSE item bank has a total of 19 items, therefore click the Duplicate button 19 times.

Scrolling down the Loop group should be duplicated 19 times.

Then click Apply to apply this flow set up to the survey.



Step 3.8 - Publish the Test/Survey

Go to ‘Survey Options’
Select ’Responses’
Uncheck the options Back Button and Allow respondents to finish later



Then go to ‘Builder’ options again, and
click ‘Publish’


After following short instructions, the survey will be published and a unique anonymous URL will be activated.

Now, the link https://uva.fra1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_1AimrTMN02GK1cW corresponds to a Qualtrics survey of the PROMIS Pediatric Psychological Stress Experiences (PPSE) item bank using computerized adaptive testing (CAT).






